{
 "id": "pqf-def-affine-morphism",
 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Affine morphisms",
 "statement": "A morphism of schemes $f:X\\to S$ is *affine* if for every affine\nopen $V\\subset S$ the preimage $f^{-1}(V)$ is affine, in the sense of\nthe ambient-foundations chapter; any morphism\nbetween affine schemes is affine, and a closed immersion is affine.\n(*Stacks Project, Morphisms of Schemes, Section 29.11, Tag\n[01S8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01S8).*)",
